Understanding the sequential layer:
------------ ---- ---------- -----
1.Flatten----> Conversion of high dimension data into low dimension data.
NOTE:
    *It creates image into one-dimensional array.
    *Image generally contains three dimensional.
       Height
       Width
       Channels(grey scale or RGB)
    *Above three dimensional will convert into single dimensional by
     shaping into height * width * channel
    *When our code contains 28*28=784pixel in our flatten layer it means our images are
     in height of 28 and width of 28.
    * 28 is not a fixed pixel value.It can change with image to image.
2.Layers of Deep Learning Sequential Process:
   1.Input Layer(Flatten)
   2.Hidden Layer(Dense(128, activation='relu'))
   3.Output Layer(Dense(10, activation='softmax'))
    NOTE:
       1.'128' inside the dense layer is called as neron
       2.Based upon the complexity of the images the dense layer can have different
         numbers(Dense(32,64,128,256,512,1024,2048))(It can be read according to hyperparameter).
       3.A sequential or input layer has many hidden layer depends upon the input.
       4.A Dense((10, activation='softmax')).No 10 indicates No.of images to be
         classified.It is very according to the input.
       5.Activation function for hidden layer and output layer can vary as we wish.
3.Model.compile:
     This step takes structure that we formed with sequential layer.
       1.Optimizer is the processing in which model updates its weights based upon the
         data exists.
       1.1.Types of Optimizer(It is an algorithm for the model to adjust various issues and produce minimum loss):
           NOTE: Minimization of the loss function.
           a.Adam
           b.SGD
           c.RMSprop
           d.Adagrad
     2.Loss Function:It is basically an algorithm to find the how the model is performing
            training.It tells you the difference between model prediction and actual.It is
            similar to the OneHotEncoding.
     3.Metric:How well the data is performed with optimizer and loss.
4.Model.Fit:
     epoch=5--->No of iteration.


